<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alvor Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angolan-war-of-independence">Angolan War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alvor Agreement was signed on 15 January 1975 at Alvor in Portugal by the Portuguese government and the three Angolan liberation movements, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpla">MPLA</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-of-angola">FNLA</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unita">UNITA</a>. It set <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>'s independence for 11 November 1975, defined Cabinda as part of Angola, and created a transitional government shared by the movements. Fighting among them soon destroyed it, opening the Angolan civil war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvor-agreement.jpg" alt="Alvor Agreement" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Portuguese government, FNLA, MPLA, UNITA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alvor_Agreement.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
